    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d412">

                <pb facs="0498" n="332" xml:id="pg332"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 818.00/169</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Chargé Johnson </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-20T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 20, 1917—5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your telegram June 15, noon. Your action therein set forth is approved. For your
                    guidance you are confidentially informed that this Government will not look with
                    approval upon any revolution in the personal interest of Gonzáles or Quesada,
                    and they have been so advised.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
